# NOTICE

Agent Delegation orchestrates locally installed Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode and
Google Antigravity (`agy`) CLIs. It performs no OAuth of its own and stores no
credentials; each CLI authenticates itself.

- Job logs, prompts, transcripts and context snapshots may contain project code
  and task text. They are stored locally and are not encrypted. Do not delegate
  prompts that contain secrets.
- `supervisor.verifyCommands` are project-configured commands executed with your
  privileges; `run` requires `--approve-all` before they can run.
- The stop-review gate is a best-effort heuristic and fails OPEN (allows
  stopping) on any timeout or parse error. It applies to the legacy agy plugin.
- The legacy agy review commands run read-only; the companion never passes
  `--dangerously-skip-permissions` for review/adversarial-review jobs.
- The bundled Claude Agent SDK is redistributed under its own license; see
  `plugins/agent-delegation/scripts/vendor/claude-agent-sdk-LICENSE.md`.
